      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Phantom limb pain following amputation is a well known but comparatively rare phenomenon. Spinal anaesthesia in amputees may cause reappearance of phantom pain in previously pain-free patients despite complete sensory analgesia. Two such cases are described."},
